<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · site</p><h1 class="enc-title">São Cucufate</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">São Cucufate is the site of a large Roman villa near Vila de Frades, in the Vidigueira municipality of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alentejo">Alentejo</a> in southern Portugal. Founded in the 1st century CE and rebuilt on a grand scale in the 4th century, its two-storey residence with vaulted halls survives to an unusual height. In the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/middle-ages">Middle Ages</a> part of it was used by a monastery dedicated to Saint Cucufas, from whom the site takes its name.</p></div>
